# Catalog iframe after git push

Whenever you push updates to the public skill catalog repo (`gptfy-agentic-skills-catalog` / GitHub Pages), **always end with the updated iframe embed code** in the same response.

## Required output after a successful push

1. Get the latest short SHA from `main` (or the commit just pushed).
2. Provide this iframe block with a cache-busting `?v=<sha>` query param:

```html
<iframe
  src="https://kalanithib94.github.io/gptfy-agentic-skills-catalog/?v=<sha>"
  title="GPTfy Agentic Skills Catalog"
  width="100%"
  height="900"
  style="border:0; border-radius:12px; min-height:720px;"
  loading="lazy"
  allow="clipboard-write"
></iframe>
```

3. Also include the plain live URL with the same `?v=<sha>` for quick copy.

Do this automatically — do not wait for the user to ask for the iframe.
